# Table §width — A COLUMN NEEDS A POSITIVE WIDTH.
#
# `width 0,auto` and `width auto,0%` drew a zero-width column, while
# `pin width=0` was already refused. RULE 4.4: a spelling shared on purpose
# shares its value grammar. Each of the four tables below has one zero
# width (`0`, `0%`, `0.0`, `0px`) and must be refused on its `width` line.
# A zero with a unit gets the same error, not the `px` hint: rewriting
# `0px` as the hint said (`0`) was refused in turn.
figdown 0.5 table
table t1 "T1"
| A | B |
|---|---|
| a | b |
width 0,auto
table t2 "T2"
| A | B |
|---|---|
| a | b |
width auto,0%
table t3 "T3"
| A | B |
|---|---|
| a | b |
width 0.0,10
table t4 "T4"
| A | B |
|---|---|
| a | b |
width 0px,auto
